      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:a33fb2688e15bc8f",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did mor mean, and what did bhaĩs mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: बर्तन",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बर्तन (bartan) — \"a cooking vessel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बर्तन (bartan) is the word that goes with बरतना (baratnā), 'to handle, to make use of', and behind both stands Sanskrit वृत् (vṛt-), 'to turn, to carry on'. A बर्तन (bartan) is, quite literally, a thing in use."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is why one word covers the whole shelf. A pot, a pan, a tray, a lid — each has its own name, and all of them together are बर्तन (bartan). Ask politely for बर्तन (bartan) and you have asked for whatever the cooking needs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five things at the fire."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bartan",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bartan*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bartan, then thālī, and say which of them is the whole shelf",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bartan*, then *thālī*, and say which of them is the whole shelf]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
