          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गिलास (gilās) — \"a tumbler\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This one is English glass, taken whole. It arrived with the object, the way कैमरा arrived with the camera, and Hindi gave it a vowel in the middle so that a Hindi mouth could get through the gl- at the front."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Watch what happened to the meaning on the way in. A Hindi गिलास (gilās) is a drinking tumbler and is very often made of steel, so the English word for the material now names an object in a language where the object is usually not made of it."
            }
          ]
        },
