          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तवा (tavā) — \"a flat iron griddle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Usually traced to a Sanskrit word on the root तप् (tap-), 'to heat, to burn' — the heater. The same root is inside तपस्, the heat of hard practice, so the kitchen and the hermitage turn out to share a syllable."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A तवा (tavā) is a flat iron disc over the fire, and it is what रोटी is made on. No तवा (tavā), no रोटी: the bread you met early on is defined by the surface it is cooked on as much as by the flour."
            }
          ]
        },
