    {
      "id": "HI-C61-stove",
      "sequence": 2300,
      "title": "चूल्हा (chūlhā) — a cooking fire",
      "headword": "चूल्हा",
      "romanization": "chūlhā",
      "gloss": "a cooking fire",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:ea606731b807dc39",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Name the 4 words of this chapter so far."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चूल्हा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चूल्हा (chūlhā) — \"a cooking fire\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit चुल्ली (cullī), 'fireplace, hearth'. The oldest चूल्हा (chūlhā) is a horseshoe of packed clay on the floor, fed with wood at the front, with the तवा (tavā) sitting on top of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It also counts households. To say two brothers have separate चूल्हे is to say they no longer eat as one family — the fire, not the roof, is what marks where one household ends. A gas ring in a city flat inherits the word and the meaning both."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: बर्तन (bartan), चम्मच (chammach), गिलास (gilās), तवा (tavā), चूल्हा (chūlhā). Enough to ask for what the cooking needs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "chūlhā",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *chūlhā*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
